From 49fc670dd88ef95d4067b5d520a9e8e36655fe5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Alef <chris@crickertech.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:51:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(rsext4): add fuzz targets for the on-disk parsers, mount
 and journal replay

Add a cargo-fuzz crate under fs/rsext4/fuzz with seven targets: the
superblock checks mount runs first, the group descriptor table, one
extent-tree node, one directory block with its checksum tails, hash-tree
lookups through a read-only mount, a bounded read-only walk of a whole
image, and a read-write mount that replays the journal. The crate has its
own workspace, so the sanitizer build stays out of the repository
workspace and xtask.

make-seeds.sh builds a small seed corpus with mke2fs and a fixed time:
1 KiB and 4 KiB blocks, with and without metadata_csum, an indexed
directory, and an image with one committed journal transaction that
e2fsck must replay.
